<title>JAPAN: No Japan bank collapses on horizon -- MOF's Ogawa.</title>
<headline>No Japan bank collapses on horizon -- MOF's Ogawa.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese Vice Finance Minister Tadashi Ogawa told a news conference on Monday that his ministry was not aware of any cases in which debt-ridden banks might be in danger of collapse.</p>
<p>Asked whether the ministry, as a result of its inspections, knew of any banks which were so seriously in the red that their survival could be in doubt, Ogawa said: &quot;Not at the moment.&quot;</p>
</text>
